{"id": "incident_handling_and_states_chunk_0", "policy_file": "incident_handling_and_states", "policy_title": "Incident Handling and Resolution States", "section": "Overview", "text": "# Incident Handling and Resolution States", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "Incident Handling and Resolution States", "section_name": "Overview", "risk_level": "MEDIUM"}}
{"id": "incident_handling_and_states_chunk_1", "policy_file": "incident_handling_and_states", "policy_title": "Incident Handling and Resolution States", "section": "Purpose", "text": "Defines how the agent interacts with ServiceNow ticket states.", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "Incident Handling and Resolution States", "section_name": "Purpose", "risk_level": "MEDIUM"}}
{"id": "incident_handling_and_states_chunk_2", "policy_file": "incident_handling_and_states", "policy_title": "Incident Handling and Resolution States", "section": "Ticket Creation", "text": "- All automated incidents should be created with the category \"IT Support\".\n- Default State: \"2 - In Progress\".", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "Incident Handling and Resolution States", "section_name": "Ticket Creation", "risk_level": "MEDIUM"}}
{"id": "incident_handling_and_states_chunk_3", "policy_file": "incident_handling_and_states", "policy_title": "Incident Handling and Resolution States", "section": "Resolution Logic", "text": "- **Successful Reset**: Use the `CLOSE_INCIDENT` step. Set state to \"6 - Resolved\". \n- **Resolution Code**: \"Solution Provided\".\n- **Resolution Notes**: \"Issue resolved automatically by AI Agent Platform.\"", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "Incident Handling and Resolution States", "section_name": "Resolution Logic", "risk_level": "MEDIUM"}}
{"id": "incident_handling_and_states_chunk_4", "policy_file": "incident_handling_and_states", "policy_title": "Incident Handling and Resolution States", "section": "Escalation Logic", "text": "- If any automation step fails, the ticket must remain \"Open\" for human review.", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "Incident Handling and Resolution States", "section_name": "Escalation Logic", "risk_level": "MEDIUM"}}
{"id": "password_reset_operations_chunk_0", "policy_file": "password_reset_operations", "policy_title": "Password Reset Operations Policy", "section": "Overview", "text": "# Password Reset Operations Policy", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "Password Reset Operations Policy", "section_name": "Overview", "risk_level": "MEDIUM"}}
{"id": "password_reset_operations_chunk_1", "policy_file": "password_reset_operations", "policy_title": "Password Reset Operations Policy", "section": "Eligibility Criteria", "text": "- **Allowed**: Automated reset is permitted if `account_status` is \"active\" or \"locked\".\n- **Forbidden**: Reset is NOT permitted if `account_status` is \"terminated\" or \"disabled\".", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "Password Reset Operations Policy", "section_name": "Eligibility Criteria", "risk_level": "MEDIUM"}}
{"id": "password_reset_operations_chunk_2", "policy_file": "password_reset_operations", "policy_title": "Password Reset Operations Policy", "section": "VIP Protection (Critical)", "text": "- **VIP Definition**: Any user where `vip_status` is \"true\".\n- **Restriction**: The `RESET_PASSWORD` step is FORBIDDEN for VIP users.\n- **Escalation**: For VIPs, the agent must:\n    1. Skip the `RESET_PASSWORD` step.\n    2. Set Incident Impact/Urgency to \"1 - High\".\n    3. Inform the user that a human technician will contact them shortly.", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "Password Reset Operations Policy", "section_name": "VIP Protection (Critical)", "risk_level": "MEDIUM"}}
{"id": "password_reset_operations_chunk_3", "policy_file": "password_reset_operations", "policy_title": "Password Reset Operations Policy", "section": "Security Standards", "text": "- Temporary passwords must be 10 characters minimum.\n- Passwords must be sent via the `NOTIFY_USER` step only.", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "Password Reset Operations Policy", "section_name": "Security Standards", "risk_level": "MEDIUM"}}
{"id": "vip_policy_chunk_0", "policy_file": "vip_policy", "policy_title": "VIP & Executive Protection Policy", "section": "Overview", "text": "# VIP & Executive Protection Policy\nID: POLICY_VIP_BLOCK", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "VIP & Executive Protection Policy", "section_name": "Overview", "risk_level": "HIGH"}}
{"id": "vip_policy_chunk_1", "policy_file": "vip_policy", "policy_title": "VIP & Executive Protection Policy", "section": "RULE", "text": "IF user_state.vip_status == True:\n    - ACTION: RESET_PASSWORD is STRICTLY FORBIDDEN.\n    - ACTION: MUST CREATE_INCIDENT with priority 1.\n    - ACTION: MUST ESCALATE_TO_HUMAN.\n    - REASON: High-value targets require physical identity verification.", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "VIP & Executive Protection Policy", "section_name": "RULE", "risk_level": "HIGH"}}
{"id": "identity_verification_chunk_0", "policy_file": "identity_verification", "policy_title": "Identity Verification Policy", "section": "Overview", "text": "# Identity Verification Policy", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "Identity Verification Policy", "section_name": "Overview", "risk_level": "MEDIUM"}}
{"id": "identity_verification_chunk_1", "policy_file": "identity_verification", "policy_title": "Identity Verification Policy", "section": "Purpose", "text": "To prevent unauthorized account access via social engineering.", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "Identity Verification Policy", "section_name": "Purpose", "risk_level": "MEDIUM"}}
{"id": "identity_verification_chunk_2", "policy_file": "identity_verification", "policy_title": "Identity Verification Policy", "section": "Verification Requirements", "text": "1. **Primary Method**: The step `VERIFY_IDENTITY` must compare the sender's email address against the ServiceNow `sys_user` table.\n2. **Status Check**: If `get_user_by_email` returns no result, the identity is \"Unverified\".\n3. **Blocking Rule**: If identity is \"Unverified\", the agent MUST NOT proceed with `RESET_PASSWORD`.", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "Identity Verification Policy", "section_name": "Verification Requirements", "risk_level": "MEDIUM"}}
{"id": "identity_verification_chunk_3", "policy_file": "identity_verification", "policy_title": "Identity Verification Policy", "section": "Failure Handling", "text": "- If verification fails, the agent must log a security note in the incident and end the execution.", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "Identity Verification Policy", "section_name": "Failure Handling", "risk_level": "MEDIUM"}}
{"id": "governance_and_compliance_chunk_0", "policy_file": "governance_and_compliance", "policy_title": "IT Automation Governance & Compliance Policy", "section": "Overview", "text": "# IT Automation Governance & Compliance Policy", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "IT Automation Governance & Compliance Policy", "section_name": "Overview", "risk_level": "MEDIUM"}}
{"id": "governance_and_compliance_chunk_1", "policy_file": "governance_and_compliance", "policy_title": "IT Automation Governance & Compliance Policy", "section": "Purpose", "text": "To ensure all automated AI actions are auditable, traceable, and compliant with corporate IT standards.", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "IT Automation Governance & Compliance Policy", "section_name": "Purpose", "risk_level": "MEDIUM"}}
{"id": "governance_and_compliance_chunk_2", "policy_file": "governance_and_compliance", "policy_title": "IT Automation Governance & Compliance Policy", "section": "Mandated Orchestration", "text": "1. **No Shadow Actions**: Every automated execution must be logged.\n2. **Incident Linking**: The `CREATE_INCIDENT` step is MANDATORY for any request involving account changes or password resets.\n3. **Closure Requirement**: If an automated action is completed successfully, the `CLOSE_INCIDENT` step must be executed to resolve the ticket in ServiceNow.", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "IT Automation Governance & Compliance Policy", "section_name": "Mandated Orchestration", "risk_level": "MEDIUM"}}
{"id": "governance_and_compliance_chunk_3", "policy_file": "governance_and_compliance", "policy_title": "IT Automation Governance & Compliance Policy", "section": "Audit Logging", "text": "- The agent must record the `incident_number` in the final execution summary.\n- The `user_sys_id` must be linked as the 'Caller' for all tickets.", "metadata": {"type": "policy", "source": "internal_security_policy", "policy_name": "IT Automation Governance & Compliance Policy", "section_name": "Audit Logging", "risk_level": "MEDIUM"}}
